 ## Runtime semantics
 
+- **Position pointer.** Every recorded tick moves `refs/quilt/HEAD` to that
+  commit. It is ordinary git data, not runtime: no `quilt-init` is needed to
+  READ it (the hook is runtime; the ref is data). `quilt-head` prints it,
+  and refuses honestly (`exit 1`, "no ticks recorded yet") on a repo with
+  zero ticks instead of guessing from `HEAD`. Honest limits: a *default*
+  `git clone` drops it (only `refs/heads/*` + tags travel); it crosses via
+  explicit refspec (`+refs/quilt/*:refs/quilt/*`) or `git bundle` — pin P8
+  nails both directions. Deliberate boundary: the hook's own
+  `quilt: cascade after ...` commits do NOT move it — the pointer tracks
+  *recorded* (receipted, watch-logged) ticks, not every commit touching
+  `cells/`.
 - **Receipts.** `post-commit` writes `.quilt/receipts/<short>.json`:
   `{commit, changed_cells, key_dials{<alias>{obstruction,freeze}}, ts}`.
   `ts` is the git commit time (`git log -1 --format=%ct`), never wall clock,
